1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
You don't need to move fast, because if you're heading in the wrong direction,

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
speed only takes you further away from where you're meant to be.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Deeper into confusion, faster into a dead end. In the journey of life,

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
no one really cares who gets there first. What truly matters is whether you get there at all.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Whether you reach your own destination, your own success. Everyone walks a different path.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Trying to compare your steps to someone else's only piles of unnecessary pressure on your shoulders.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
It makes you anxious, distracted, and sometimes even lost.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
What counts isn't how quickly you move, but how long you can endure.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
How deeply you're willing to commit. Because progress isn't a sprint, it's a test of patience

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:51,000
and persistence. There are those who take off early, blazing ahead, but burn out or give up

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
along the way. And there are others who start slowly, cautiously. But every step they take is

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,000
solid, intentional, unwavering. You don't need to outpace anyone else. You just need to be a

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
little stronger, a little wiser, a little better than the person you were yesterday. You don't need

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
to run. You just need to keep walking, steadily, purposefully, in the right direction. In the end,

15
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:27,000
it's not the one who arrives first who wins, it's the one who refuses to stop.

